<title>USA: Mobile Mini Inc Q1 profit.</title>
<headline>Mobile Mini Inc Q1 profit.</headline>
<dateline>TEMPE, Ariz. 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three Months Ended</p>
<p>						    March 31</p>
<p>						 1997	     1996</p>
<p> Revenues			     $9,649,456     $8,908,915</p>
<p>Net income (loss) before</p>
<p> extraordinary item		    201,762	(113,968)</p>
<p> Extraordinary item (1)		    N/A	(410,354)</p>
<p> Net income (loss)		     201,762	(524,322)</p>
<p>Net income (loss) per common</p>
<p>and common share equivalent</p>
<p> before extraordinary item		 .03	    (.02)</p>
<p> Extraordinary item (1)		    N/A	    (.06)</p>
<p>Net income (loss) per common</p>
<p> and common share equivalent	     .03	    (.08)</p>
<p>Weighted average shares</p>
<p> outstanding			   6,739,758	6,732,358</p>
<p>(1): On March 29, 1996, the Company entered into a credit agreement with BT Commercial Corporation consisting of $35 million revolving line of credit and a $6 million term loan. In connection with the closing of the credit agreement, the Company terminated its existing credit line and repaid other long-term debt.  As a result, prepayment penalties and previously deferred costs related to certain indebtedness resulted in an extraordinary charge to earnings in the first quarter of 1996 of approximately $410,000, or $.06 per share, after the benefit for income taxes.</p>
